Package: wsgnstat
Type: Package
Title: The Wrapped Skew Generalised Normal Distribution
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("M. Theodor", "Loots", email = "theo.loots@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7722-3913"))
Description: The skew generalised normal distribution on the line, constructed as a scale mixture of
    a uniform and a generalised gamma variable, and its wrapped version on the circle, with density,
    distribution and quantile functions, characteristic function, trigonometric moments, random
    generation, and estimation by the method of trigonometric moments (minimum distance, with
    sandwich standard errors) and by maximum likelihood. The characteristic function is evaluated
    through absolutely convergent integrals (the Fox H-function route), so every routine is
    available for all positive shape parameters, not only where the Fox-Wright series converges.
    A pure-C back-end does the numerics and also backs the 'Python' package 'wsgnstat'.
URL: https://github.com/mtloots/wsgnstat
BugReports: https://github.com/mtloots/wsgnstat/issues
